# Project foundation

- Phase 002 is complete with the original five groups plus one accepted post-exit addendum: **Propagation Safeguard**. Current accepted concept count: **21**.
- **Phase 003 is active. Groups 01–03 are accepted; Group 04 — Lineage, Investigation & Causal Reasoning is next.**
- Work remains documentation/design-first unless the user explicitly advances into technical/implementation design.
- Do not create application code, notebooks, infrastructure, schemas, APIs, deployment workflows, quarantine implementations, or prototypes prematurely.
- Treat `docs/` as the product/design system of record.
- Before Phase 003 changes, read the phase index, synchronization template, active group, accepted participating concept specs/addenda, glossary, foundation, and decisions.
- Preserve concept ownership boundaries; synchronization coordinates concepts rather than merging them.
- Synchronization is not automatically an API call, workflow, transaction, event, message bus, database relation, or service boundary.
- Synchronization order is never authority; a trigger is never causation.
- One unresolved branch must not erase independently valid results.
- Treat execution timing/dependency latency as first-class health evidence distinct from DQ.
- Prospective Impact is not actual Impact.
- Analyst Investigation remains first-class; automatic escalation requires explicit accepted criteria.
- Propagation Safeguard proposal/activation/release remain separate from Assessment and causality.
- Refine canonical docs rather than creating duplicates.
- Never silently choose graph/event/ledger/quarantine/workflow/service architecture.
- Treat the multi-repository Databricks environment as one reasoning ecosystem while preserving provenance boundaries.
